{title: We Seemed Like Grasshoppers}
{subtitle: Numbers 13:22–33; 14:1–3; Deuteronomy 1:28; Numbers 14:24; Joshua 14:12–15; 11:21–22}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Cm7] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Through the Negev they climbed to the [Cm7]land
Where the giants of Hebron [Eb]stood tall
Ahiman Sheshai and Talmai
[Cm7]The descendants of Anak re[Abmaj7]mained there
A single clus[Eb]ter of grapes
Carried on a pole [Abmaj7]by two
Forty days they scouted the [Eb]place
And brought [Bb/D]back the fruit [Cm7]of [Abmaj7]the land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
It flows with milk and [Bb]honey indeed
[Cm]But the cities are [Gm7]strong and the people [Abmaj7]great
The walls rise up [Bb]to the sky
[Abmaj7]And our hearts have melt[Bb]ed [Eb]in fear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
We saw the descendants of A[Cm7]nak
The Nephilim from whom they [Abmaj7]came
In our own eyes we seemed like [Bb]grasshoppers
So we [Abmaj7]seemed to [Bb]them we [Eb]said
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The whole congregation wept that night
Grumbling a[Cm7]gainst Moses and Aaron
Why bring us [Eb]here to fall by the sword
[Ebmaj7/D]Our [Cm7]wives and children become plunder
If [Abmaj7]only we had died in the wilderness
Or [Eb]back in Egypt we wished
[Abmaj7]But one man stood with a different spirit
[Eb]Caleb who [Bb/D]followed whole[Cm7]heartedly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]We saw the descendants of Anak [Ebmaj7/D]
[Cm7]The Nephilim from whom they came
[Abmaj7]In our own eyes we seemed like [Bb]grasshoppers
So we [Abmaj7]seemed to [Bb]them we [Eb]said
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Abmaj7]Joshua cut off the Anakim
From [Eb]Hebron Debir and Anab
Devot[Abmaj7]ing them to destruction
So [Eb]none remained in the hill country
[Abmaj7]Only in Gaza Gath and Ashdod
Did [Eb]any of them survive
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
But [Abmaj7]Caleb drove out the [Bb]three
[Abmaj7]Sheshai Ahiman and Tal[Bb]mai
[Abmaj7]Hebron was called [Bb]Ki-riath-ar-ba
[Abmaj7]After the [Bb]greatest among [Eb]them
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
